hadiths[19]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1930","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever drank alcohol in the world and did not repent, he will be deprived of (pure, that is, the pure wine of Paradise) in the Hereafter."
"1931","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The adulterer, at the time of committing adultery, is not a believer; and the one who drinks alcohol, at the time of drinking, is not a believer; and the thief, at the time of stealing, is not a believer."
"1932","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) in another narration: ""In the same way, when a thief commits a major robbery such that people raise their eyes to look at him, then at that time (i.e., while stealing) he is also not a believer."
"1933","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about ""bit‘"" which is an intoxicating drink made from honey, and the people of Yemen used to drink it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Every intoxicating drink is forbidden."
"1934","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Amir Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""There will be some groups in my Ummah who will consider adultery, wearing silk, drinking wine, and musical instruments as lawful, and there will be some groups who will live on the side of a mountain. In the evening, when their shepherd brings their herd to them, a poor person will come to them and ask for his need. They will reply, '(Not today) come tomorrow.' So Allah Almighty will destroy them that very night and cause the mountain to fall upon them, and the rest will be transformed (metamorphosed) into monkeys and pigs. They will remain in this punishment of Allah until the Day of Resurrection."
"1935","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Usaid As-Sa'idi (may Allah be pleased with him) that he invited the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his wedding (and at that time) his wife, who was the bride, kept serving all the people. He said, ""Do you know what the bride gave the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to drink?"" She had soaked some dates in a bowl overnight (and served that drink)."
"1936","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade soaking nabidh (date drink) in containers other than water skins, the people said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that water skins are not available to everyone (what should they do?). So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted soaking nabidh in all containers except those coated with pitch."
"1937","Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mixing unripe and ripe dates together, and mixing dates and grapes together for soaking; rather, each of them should be soaked separately (then there is no harm)."
"1938","Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Abu Humayd Ansari brought milk to the Prophet (peace be upon him) in a bowl from the place of Naqi’. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to him: “Why did you not cover it? (At least) you could have placed a broad wooden board over it.”"
"1939","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The best charity is to give a she-camel with abundant milk to someone (in the way of Allah) to drink its milk, and likewise to give a goat with abundant milk, so that it fills one vessel with milk in the morning and another in the evening."
"1940","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to an Ansari, and a companion (Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him) was with him. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to that person: ""If you have water from the night (stale) in your waterskin, then serve it (from a vessel), otherwise we will drink directly from the trough."" (The narrator) says that this person was watering his garden (that is why the Prophet, peace be upon him, said this). That person submitted, ""Please come to the hut, I have water from the night (stale) (I will bring it)."" So he took both of them there and brought water in a bowl and milk from his goat, which he milked into it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) drank it, then the one who had come with him also drank."
"1941","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that he came to the door of the platform (in the mosque of Kufa) and drank while standing, then said: ""Indeed, some people consider it disliked to drink water while standing, whereas I myself saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drinking in this manner, just as you have seen me drinking."
"1942","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) drank Zamzam water while standing."
"1943","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade turning the water-skin upside down (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, forbade drinking water from the mouth of the water-skin by turning it over)."
"1944","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking from the mouth (opening) of a water-skin or water-bag (the narrator is unsure), and also forbade that anyone should prevent his neighbor from driving a peg into his wall."
"1945","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to breathe three times while drinking water."
"1946","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever drinks (or eats) from a silver vessel, indeed he is filling his belly with the fire of Hell."
"1947","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of Banu Sa’ida and said: “O Sahl! Give us water to drink.” I brought out that bowl and gave water to him (the Prophet, peace be upon him) in it. The narrator says that Sayyiduna Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) brought out the same bowl for us and we drank from it. After that, ‘Umar bin ‘Abd al-‘Aziz (may Allah have mercy on him) requested that bowl as a gift, so he gave it to him."
"1948","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that he had the cup of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He says that I gave water to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this cup for a long time. (The narrator) says that there was an iron ring in this cup. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) wished to replace it with a silver or gold ring, but Sayyiduna Abu Talha (may Allah be pleased with him) said (upon hearing this), ""Do not change what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has made."" So Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) left it as it was."
